//? Title: Stone SIP: actual incomplete factors and matching final residuals
//? Subtitle: Actual canonical histories, retained original fixtures and explicit controls
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Strongly implicit procedure approximately factors a five-point grid operator,
then corrects its iterate using residual solves. The report retains the
original30 by30 Poisson fixture and exposes actual factor intermediates and
correction histories.
)

\toc

> Mechanism and mathematical scope

For each row-major cell, factor the west/south lower terms and normalized
east/north upper terms, cancelling a fraction alpha of the diagonal fill
effects. For current x compute r=b-Ax, solve the incomplete lower/upper
triangular systems for delta, and update x<-x+delta. The native history
recomputes the Euclidean residual after every completed correction.
Factorization is approximate: arbitrary matrices need not converge, residuals
need not decrease monotonically and a small residual alone is not an
unconditional forward-error certificate. Zero pivots and invalid factor
denominators fail explicitly.

> A tiny actual producing history

The table and native concept diagram read the same producing execution. Every
block below is a complete editable C++ program.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/stone_sip_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    namespace a = dm::algorithms;
    namespace g = dm::graphics;
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto grid = a::stone_poisson_example(2, 2);
    auto r = a::stone_sip_trace(grid);
    std::print("| actual cell | Lw | Ls | Lp | Ue | Un |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < r.Lp.size(); ++i)
        std::print("| {} | {:.9g} | {:.9g} | {:.9g} | {:.9g} | {:.9g} |\n", i,
                   r.Lw[i], r.Ls[i], r.Lp[i], r.Ue[i], r.Un[i]);
    std::print("Completed {} corrections; matching final residual {:.9g}; converged {}.\n",
               r.result.iterations, r.result.residual, r.converged);
    g::Diagram concept_diagram(48, 1100);
    concept_diagram.node("n0", {0, 0},
                         std::format("{} actual factored cells",
                                     r.factorized_cells));
    concept_diagram.node("n1", {5, 0},
                         std::format("{} completed corrections",
                                     r.result.iterations));
    concept_diagram.node("n2", {10, 0},
                         std::format("Final residual {:.3g}", r.result.residual));
    concept_diagram.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
    concept_diagram.save_svg("build/stone_sip_tiny.svg");
}
```
