> API and interpretation

Complete coefficient lengths, finite values and boundary zeros are required.
Alpha is finite in[0,1), tolerance finite nonnegative and correction cap
nonnegative. Empty grids return empty converged results; even zero-cap nonempty
runs validate/factor before checking the zero iterate. The corrected result
reports actual completed corrections and residual of the returned x, fixing the
old cap1 mismatch. Known fixture solutions are diagnostic and never read by the
solver.

Reusable producers, fixtures and histories live in the canonical C++ library.
Captured records own their values and do not come from a separate report replay.
Selected counters and record/scalar policies are specified at their API
boundaries; they are not peak-byte or wall-time budgets. Synthetic structural
inputs are controlled fixtures for these mechanisms.

> References

- [Stone, Iterative Solution of Implicit Approximations of Multidimensional Partial Differential Equations, SIAM Journal on Numerical Analysis5 (1968),530-558|https://doi.org/10.1137/0705044]

